# ~/.config/atlas-watchdog/watchdog.env on the WATCHDOG box (the Spark), mode 0600.
# (As root the path is /etc/atlas-watchdog/watchdog.env.) Never commit the real file.
#
# Miro's Slack INCOMING WEBHOOK, created for this purpose only; it lives in this
# one file and nowhere else. It is not ATLAS's bot token: a bot-token style
# value is refused. Without this line the watchdog logs
# "no alternate route configured" and exits 2 on every run.
# Form: https://hooks.slack.com/services/<T-id>/<B-id>/<secret>
ATLAS_WATCHDOG_WEBHOOK=
#
# Or, with no webhook: post via the Slack bot token into one alerts channel
# (a bot token only; used when ATLAS_WATCHDOG_WEBHOOK is empty).
# ATLAS_WATCHDOG_SLACK_TOKEN=
# ATLAS_WATCHDOG_SLACK_CHANNEL=
#
# The URL to read: the Mac's api through the reverse tunnel
# (ops/watchdog/host/watchdog_tunnel.sh). The old public https route is a
# static Caddy answer and does not prove ATLAS is alive. It must be reachable here. agency.storefront.test is the
# only public name; /healthz answers there ONLY once the Caddyfile.public route
# ships (until then it is 404, see docs/watchdog.md). Placeholder:
ATLAS_WATCHDOG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz
#
# Optional (defaults shown):
# ATLAS_WATCHDOG_TLS_WARN_DAYS=14
# ATLAS_WATCHDOG_HEARTBEAT_MAX_S=900
# ATLAS_WATCHDOG_LABEL=cloudhost-spark
